  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nThe shortwave trough, accompanied by a closed low embedded \nwithin, will continue to progress slowly eastward over Upstate \nNY and New England through the end of the work week. \nNorthwesterly flow on the backside of the trough will support a \nrenewed potential for showers in the mountains Wednesday \nafternoon. Updrafts may struggle to reach heights high enough to\nproduce lightning due to the depletion of CAPE and increasing \nsubsidence aloft; however, lightning cannot be ruled out \nentirely across the mountains. Otherwise, a refreshing, \nnorthwesterly breeze is forecast area-wide Wednesday, with \nstratocu developing by late Wednesday morning. Dry and warm \nweather is forecast through Friday, with storm chances forecast \nto return this weekend due to a shortwave trough digging into \nthe Upper Midwest as the subtropical ridge retrogrades over the \nDesert Southwest.",
